## Reference first

Read `docs/OPTICA-THEME-REFERENCE.md` before structural changes (new sections, PDP block order, header/footer wiring, CSS scope).

---

## Liquid and schema patterns

- Schema-driven sections: settings and blocks in `{% schema %}`, not hardcoded merchant copy.
- Prefer blocks over duplicated markup; use Liquid conditionals instead of copy-paste variants.
- Avoid inline styles unless required for dynamic values (e.g. per-block colors from settings).
- Section/snippet markup should be readable; keep nesting shallow.

### Naming conventions (new work)

| Kind | Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| OPTICA section | `sections/optica-{feature}.liquid` | `optica-split-hero.liquid` |
| Atelier section | `sections/atelier-{feature}.liquid` | `atelier-newsletter.liquid` |
| OPTICA block | `blocks/optica-{feature}.liquid` | `optica-wishlist-button.liquid` |
| Atelier block | `blocks/atelier-{feature}.liquid` | `atelier-lens-select.liquid` |
| Snippets | `snippets/optica-*` or `snippets/atelier-*` | `optica-breadcrumbs.liquid` |
| CSS classes | BEM-style with prefix: `optica-`, `atelier-` | `.optica-trust-bar__item` |
| Schema labels | Clear merchant-facing English; `id` in `snake_case` | `"id": "heading_text"` |

Do not rename existing `id`, `type`, or template JSON keys to match new naming — only apply conventions to **new** artifacts.

---

## Performance

- Reuse existing classes and CSS before adding new rules.
- Avoid extra wrapper divs; prefer flex/grid on existing structure.
- Do not add JS unless behavior cannot be done in CSS/Liquid.
- When JS is required, prefer small theme-owned files (e.g. `assets/auto-close-details.js`) over editing Horizon cart/product bundles.
- Defer non-critical images; avoid loading heavy assets on templates that do not need them.

---

## UX consistency (OPTICA luxury)

- Generous whitespace, clear type hierarchy, restrained gold accents.
- Buttons and CTAs should match patterns in `atelier-luxury.css` (homepage/header) and `optica-pdp.css` (PDP).
- Do not introduce new button styles when an existing pattern can be extended with a scoped modifier class.

---

## Common change routing

| Goal | Start here |
|---|---|
| Homepage section order / copy | `templates/index.json` + Theme Editor |
| PDP block order / lens flow | `templates/product.json` |
| Header layout / logo / menu | `sections/header-group.json` |
| Header look (all pages) | `assets/atelier-luxury.css` under `body.atelier-optica` |
| Homepage-only look | `assets/atelier-luxury.css` under `body.template-index` |
| PDP look | `assets/optica-pdp.css` under `body.template-product` |
| Global colors / fonts | Theme settings → `config/settings_data.json` (merchant-first) |
| New PDP capability | New `blocks/*` + register in `blocks/_product-details.liquid` |

---

## Pre-edit checklist (quick)

- [ ] Change type identified (style / layout / component)
- [ ] Target file is in **Prefer** or **Allowed** tier (see `shopify-theme.mdc`)
- [ ] Correct CSS scope prefix chosen
- [ ] Schema IDs and JSON keys will remain stable

---

## Post-edit checklist (quick)

- [ ] JSON valid; no orphaned block/setting references
- [ ] New CSS scoped; no unscoped layout/color rules
- [ ] Theme Editor settings still make sense (labels, defaults, blocks list)
- [ ] Dynamic sources and metafields still wired (reviews, prescription, wishlist URL, etc.)
